# In-Memory Search Engine & Document Indexer (Mini-Search)

The goal is to build a "Google-caliber" in-memory search engine from scratch using C++. This project relies heavily on combining multiple advanced data structures (Tries, Hash Maps, Priority Queues, Graphs, Bloom Filters) to achieve highly optimized searching, autocompletion, and ranking.

By proving why a specific data structure solves a specific scaling bottleneck, this project clearly demonstrates architectural mastery of Data Structures and Algorithms.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]  
